React Compiler was documented as "pinned exact" (CLAUDE.md, ADR) but never enabled: no `reactCompiler` setting, no plugin dependency. This PR enables it.

- `reactCompiler: true` in `apps/web/next.config.ts` (top-level option in Next 16.4.3; default `infer` mode, no reason to change).
- `babel-plugin-react-compiler` 1.0.0 (latest, published 2025-10-07, far past the 24h age rule), exact, in the pnpm catalog.
- `docs/stack-decision.md` records the actual state. CLAUDE.md untouched (now true). No `use no memo` needed, so no dev-notes entry.
- Rollback: delete the `reactCompiler: true` line (the dependency is then unused and can go in a follow-up).

Bailouts: `npx react-compiler-healthcheck@1.0.0 --src "src/**/*.tsx"` in apps/web: compiled 270 of 270 components, no incompatible libraries, no Rules-of-React violations flagged. No code changes needed. Not added as a dependency (one-off; the owner may want the eslint plugin later).

| | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| `pnpm build:web` (wall) | ~16 s | ~21 s (Next "Compiled" 8.0 s -> 8.8 s) |
| apps/web unit tests | 269 files / 4262 tests, 437.7 s | same pass count, 386.4 s |
| Harness | 382 passed, 14 skipped, 3.2 min | same, 3.6 min |
| /tvaryny HTML | 159,548 B (budget 210,000) | 159,870 B |
| Animal page HTML | 78,459 B (budget 82,000) | 78,461 B |
| All client JS+CSS in .next/static, raw / gzip | 2,094,000 / 668,738 | 2,318,820 / 773,296 (+10.7% / +15.6%) |
| First-load JS /tvaryny (client-reference-manifest chunks), raw / gz | 234,247 / 77,520 | 260,799 / 91,034 |
| /tvaryny/gortaty | 230,852 / 78,862 | 252,857 / 89,289 |
| /tvaryny/[animalId] | 210,460 / 71,123 | 227,069 / 79,197 |
| /kabinet | 120,080 / 40,759 | 123,219 / 42,361 |

Note: Turbopack's build output prints no first-load JS column; the per-route numbers are chunks listed in each route's client-reference manifest, measured the same way before and after. The compiler adds a real client-JS cost (about +105 KB gzip total, +10-14 KB gzip on the gallery and animal routes) for runtime memoization; the owner should weigh that against the render savings. No existing bundle or 'use client' allowlist guard tripped.

Behaviour: swipe deck, useAnchored/Popover/Tooltip, mascot-fit, gallery overlay, likes store and kabinet forms: all their unit tests and harness specs pass unchanged; no behaviour difference found. One harness start hit a Node `X509` assertion crash in the build worker (Windows, unrelated to the config); the rerun was clean.

`pnpm check` equivalents run: typecheck, unit tests (all packages), build:web, harness. Biome run on changed files only (`--diagnostic-level=error`).
